// Every piece of authored CONTENT in this mission lives in this one file. story.mast holds
// only the logic that reacts to it.
//
// The shape is a table of contents: one `#` root, a `##` section per loader, and `###` /
// `####` records inside. story.mast parses this once and hands each section to its loader.
//
// A record is `### [Display Name](key)`, an optional `---` fenced block of fields, then
// body prose. Comments are `//` - note that .mast uses `#` instead.

# [The Quiet Lantern](sample_mission)

// ---- Words this file shares with story.mast. Keep this list true.
// ROLE    derelict          worn by Lantern Nine
// ROLE    ghost_ship        worn by Lantern Nine
// ROLE    lifeboat          worn by The Keeper's Skiff, a landmark in this file
// ROLE    tug               worn by the Tender Osprey, once it arrives
// SIGNAL  ghost_ship_found  said when a ship comes within 2000 of Lantern Nine
// SIGNAL  derelict_scanned  said when Science scans anything that wears derelict
// SIGNAL  tug_arrived       said twenty seconds after Wait for the Tender starts


// ---- Quests. Nested records are steps of the arc above them, addressed `arc/step`.
## [Quests](quests)

### [The Dark Beacon](first_contact)
---
Arc
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
---
Lantern Nine has marked the edge of Kessel Deep for forty years. Last night she went dark.

#### [Find the Lantern](find)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
Done when: signal ghost_ship_found
Then: reveal first_contact/study
---
Fly out to the edge of the Deep and find Lantern Nine.

#### [Read the Lantern](study)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: revealed
Done when: signal derelict_scanned
---
Science should take a full scan of the beacon.

### [The Keeper](salvage)
---
Arc
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
Fails when: 10 minutes
Win: The keeper is home, and Lantern Nine will burn again.
Lose: The storm closed over the Deep with the keeper still out there.
---
A storm front is ten minutes out. One woman keeps Lantern Nine, and she is not answering. Find her and bring her in.

#### [Come Alongside](approach)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
Objective: Close to within 500 of Lantern Nine
Done when: reach derelict 500
Reward: 100 credits
Then: reveal salvage/boat
Part of: salvage
Required: true
---
The lantern is not answering hails. Bring the ship in close and take a look.

#### [Find the Skiff](boat)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: revealed
Objective: Get within 500 of the keeper's skiff
Done when: reach lifeboat 500
Reward: 100 credits
Then: reveal salvage/tug
Part of: salvage
Required: true
---
The keeper's quarters are empty, and her work skiff is gone from its cradle. Find the skiff.

#### [Wait for the Tender](tug)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: revealed
Objective: Hold near the skiff until the tender arrives
Done when: signal tug_arrived
Reward: 50 credits
Then: reveal salvage/home
Part of: salvage
Required: true
---
Marrow Station is sending a tender to take the skiff in tow. Stay with her until it gets here.

#### [Bring Her Home](home)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: revealed
Objective: Return to within 1000 of Marrow Station
Done when: reach station 1000
Reward: 200 credits
Part of: salvage
Required: true
---
The keeper is aboard and half frozen. Get her back to Marrow Station.

#### [First on Scene](quick)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
Objective: Reach Lantern Nine inside two minutes
Done when: reach derelict 500
Fails when: 2 minutes
Reward: 50 credits
---
Optional. Marrow Station pays a bonus for a fast approach.

// ---- Science scans. `Scan of:` names a ROLE, so one record covers every object wearing
// it. `Tab:` picks which science tab the text lands in, and each `%` line is one of
// several readings picked at random - so a second scan does not read identically.
## [Scans](scans)

### [Lantern Hull](derelict_scan)
---
Scan of: derelict
Tab: scan
---
% The lamp housing is cold. Nothing has burned here since last night.
% The tower is whole and every port is dark. The lamp did not fail. It was put out.

### [Lantern Materials](derelict_mat)
---
Scan of: derelict
Tab: mat
---
% Ice on the lee side, a hand thick. The storm has been here once already.

### [Lantern Intel](derelict_intel)
---
Scan of: ghost_ship
Tab: intel
---
% The keeper's last entry reads: lamp out by my own hand, gone to see what it was calling in.

### [Lantern Life Signs](derelict_bio)
---
Scan of: derelict
Tab: bio
---
% No life signs. One suit hook in the lock is empty.
% No life signs. The stove is still warm.
% One faint reading in the galley. It is a cat, and it is furious.

### [Skiff Hull](lifeboat_scan)
---
Scan of: lifeboat
Tab: scan
---
% A work skiff, cold and drifting. Her running lights are off and her tether is cut.

### [Skiff Intel](lifeboat_intel)
---
Scan of: lifeboat
Tab: intel
---
% One life sign aboard, slow and steady. She is asleep, or close to it.


// ---- Places. Each record is one thing on the map. `Roles:` is the label quests and
// scans point at, `Art:` is what it looks like, and `Loc:` is where it sits.
## [Landmarks](landmarks)

### [The Keeper's Skiff](lifeboat)
---
Kind: wreck
Roles: lifeboat
Art: wreck
Loc: 6000, 0, 6000
---
The keeper's work skiff. She took it out alone, last night, with the lamp dark behind her.
